    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-upside core led by **Gunnar Henderson** (76.04) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and presumed high-leverage spots in the lineup. Despite facing a formidable arm in Gerrit Cole, **Gunnar Henderson** projects as our cornerstone play; his ability to handle right-handed pitching provides a major boost to his floor, mitigating the danger posed by the opposing starter. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an enviable position against Kyle Bradish, with a strong platoon dynamic and a projected #3 slot that maximizes his run-production potential. **Heliot Ramos** (66.19) rounds out our top-tier tier, leveraging that same advantageous environment in the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's lineup was the exclusion of **Nasim Nunez** (38.21), who fell just shy of the threshold. While **Nasim Nunez** remains a vital asset for his elite stolen base potential, his projection cratered against an elite arm like Jacob deGrom, coupled with a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppresses his counting stat efficiency. We opted to prioritize the reliable volume of **Drake Baldwin** (65.45) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.13), both of whom benefit from superior order placement and softer matchups than what **Nasim Nunez** would face. \n\nInvestors should monitor the status of **Wade Meckler** (53.18) and **Coby Mayo** (46.68); because their scores rely on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions, any deviation in their confirmed batting order could necessitate a late-minute adjustment. Furthermore, **Luis Lara** (41.14) remains in the lineup as a marginal start, though his value is tethered to a difficult matchup against Kirby. As we monitor the wire, keep in mind that **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remain sidelined, leaving our active roster\u2014including secondary depth pieces like **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Liam Hicks**\u2014to shoulder the load in this crucial 5x5 Roto push.",
